 ## Overview
-Surface-based rendering creates an intermediate geometric representation by applying a surface detector to sample data, fitting geometric primitives to the detected surfaces, and rendering those primitives [S1, unofficial]. It differs from volume rendering by converting scalar fields into explicit meshes, and from direct voxel rendering by using compact geometric primitives rather than opaque cubes [S1, unofficial].
